From b401968ce2184459473a4d292cacaad16ea06790 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 23:06:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel: OpenMP backend, Kokkos backend for material
 properties, shared entry points

- behaviours: entry points shared by the backends (integrateBatch,
  executeInitializeFunctionOnBatch, executePostProcessingOnBatch,
  rotateBatch), each backend only binding its primitive to its options
- behaviours: OpenMP backend, offloading to the default device or using
  the threads of the host (offload option, given as a template argument)
- material properties: Kokkos and OpenMP backends; kernel selection,
  declarations of the captured variables and kernels shared by the
  backends based on the C++ programming model (no init-captures, refused
  by nvcc in extended lambdas)
- configurations openmp-host-gcc and openmp-offload-nvhpc-gpu (the latter
  is affected by two defects of nvc++ 25.11, see the documentation)
- material properties tests shared by the stlpar, openmp and kokkos
  backends (test-cxx.cxx)
